  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nThe figure shows a surface $X Y$ separating two transparent media, medium-1 and medium-2. The lines $a b$ and $c d$ represent wavefronts of a light wave travelling in medium-1 and incident on $X Y$. The lines ef and $g h$ represent wavefronts of the light wave in medium-2 after refraction.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/tm_QoNKNACdV0vkT1URUx9Z9uiV2_apI_Zxl1TkT2TA.original.fullsize.png\"><br><strong>Question:</strong>\nLight travels as a",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9zb1g",
      "text": "\nparallel beam in each medium\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9lE2t",
      "text": "\nconvergent beam in each medium\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tQU8X",
      "text": "\ndivergent beam in each medium\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OO2hk",
      "text": "\ndivergent beam in one medium and convergent beam in the other medium",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Wavefronts are parallel in both media. Therefore, light which is perpendicular to wavefront travels as a parallel beam in each medium. Hence, the correct option is (a).",
    "image": null
  },
